The Nirik Legion

[en.C18_fascism_ADJ]
Nirik

[en.C18_fascism_party]
Nirik

[en.C18_DESC]
Niriks and Kirins, two sides of the same coin: when facing anger and danger, the Kirins will awaken their inner Niriks, devouring everything with their flames; and when the scorched land is reborn, the Kirins will return with hope and flowers once again.\n\nFive years ago, guided by the map of friendship, Applejack and Fluttershy knocked on the door of the archaic country Kirins living in. With their help, Autumn Blaze managed to end the “Silence” that had lasted for decades in the Kirin country, convinced Rain Shine to start planning for the future of the Kirins.\nUnder Autumn Blaze’s guidance, the Kirin country spent five years cultivating and expanding the planting of “Foal’s Breath” — a rare flower with a long growth cycle, the only antidote to the “Silence”. Only until recently, the Kirin country has gradually lifted the “Silence” from west to east across the country, and Autumn Blaze is finally ready to formally take over Rain Shine’s scepter and lead the Kirins into the future. But when the Kirins finally completed their domestic reform and looked back at the outside world, they only saw a fragmented world.\n\nPerhaps, the Kirins should have slept longer, rather than waking up early from their dreams?

[en.PIHC_WS_C18_desc]
Niriks and Kirins, two sides of the same coin: when facing anger and danger, the Kirins will awaken their inner Niriks, devouring everything with their flames; and when the scorched land is reborn, the Kirins will return with hope and flowers once again.\nThis cycle has been repeating for thousands of years, and the Kirin tribe has never had much contact with the outside world, nor have they ever established a stable civilization.\n\nDecades ago, another Kirin leader abdicated after Nirik Rebellion. On the wasteland, a singing star welcomed by all Kirins, Rain Shine, was elected as the new leader. Another cycle is about to begin, and she decided to change the fate of the Kirin country in her own way: she gave up her singing career, gave up her voice, and implemented a creative “Silence” across the country: “If there is no quarrel, there will be no anger.” The disappearance of language, character, poetry, drama... all communication and creation, finally brought peace to the Kirin country. The Kirin country enjoyed stability and development for decades for the first time — but is it worth it? Even Rain Shine herself was troubled by the “Silence”. Still, all Kirins had accepted this price: it was worth it, because this might be the only way out.\n\nHowever, the cycles of the Kirin country for thousands of years have not been in vain. Each generation of Kirin leaders has passed down their wisdom and power, and let the next, more outstanding Kirin inherit the leadership. And the next leader is Autumn Blaze.\nFive years ago, guided by the map of friendship, Applejack and Fluttershy knocked on the door of the archaic country Kirins living in. With their help, Autumn Blaze managed to end the “Silence” that had lasted for decades in the Kirin country, convinced Rain Shine to start planning for the future of the Kirins.\n“Anger can be controlled” is the belief of this leader-to-be. Autumn Blaze believes that the Kirin country does not need to choose between silence and rebellion. This is not a new idea, as many Kirin leaders have tried it over the years, but ultimately, civilization has vanished in flames. However, this time is different, as ponies and other creatures have established communication channels across the world through the School of Friendship. Kirins will no longer be alone. Ponies and other creatures will help them face future challenges together. Just like the demonstration that Applejack and Fluttershy made, as long as the Kirins introduce the concept of friendship, the historical cycle of the Kirin country will no longer repeat.\n\nUnder Autumn Blaze’s guidance, the Kirin country spent five years cultivating and expanding the planting of “Foal’s Breath” — a rare flower with a long growth cycle, the only antidote to the “Silence”. Only until recently, the Kirin country has gradually lifted the “Silence” from west to east across the country, and Autumn Blaze is finally ready to formally take over Rain Shine’s scepter and lead the Kirins into the future. But when the Kirins finally completed their domestic reform and looked back at the outside world, they only saw a fragmented world.\n\nPerhaps, “friendship” is not as powerful as it was advertised a few years ago? Perhaps, the Kirins should have slept longer, rather than waking up early from their dreams?

